+When `DISCORD_MENTION_ID` holds a valid Discord snowflake (17–20 digits, as shown in
+Discord's *Copy User ID*), each alert ends with `<@ID>` on its own line, which
+triggers a push notification. The value is validated strictly: anything else
+(including `@everyone`, `@here`, names, or IDs with extra characters) is ignored
+silently, so a misconfigured mention can never become a mass ping. The 1800-character
+cap includes the mention, so long alerts are truncated before it and the ping always
+survives.
